feat 1.0

# SPEC-ADPMEM-001 — the memory adapter's two optional window methods: peekCapture
# (ADR-0020, non-destructive) and settle (ADR-0021, the fence), plus its declaration of
# which observation modes it serves (SPEC-RT-002). Agreed and ordered built by Sift decision 58a4ac88
# (2026-11-09: "flip them, queue in that order").
#
# The spec is driven through a probe, adapters/memory/fixtures/probe.mjs (part of the build,
# inside touches, not shipped in the package). `ObserveMemory { script }` creates the adapter
# with two consumers (fixtures/consumers.mjs: Ping publishes Pong, as in the conformance
# suite) and runs the script, a space-separated list of steps: `seed`, `deliver:<Event>`,
# `start`, `peek`, `settle`, `stop`, `reset`. It answers a `trace` (each step, with the count of
# records for peek/stop and true/false for settle), `lastTypes` (the record types of the last
# peek or stop, comma-joined) and `peekEqualsStop` (the last peek and the next stop returned
# deeply equal arrays; absent when the script has no peek followed by a stop).
#
# Why settle may vouch here: every write the memory adapter can see is a synchronous push onto
# its log, issued by the adapter itself (seed) or by a consumer the adapter awaits (deliver).
# After the harness has awaited deliver, nothing is queued but work a consumer detached from
# its own promise, which no fence can see (ADR-0021: writes started after the handler returned
# are outside the fence) — so settle yields the event loop once and then vouches, and it
# declines when no capture window is open (there is nothing to vouch for).

spec SPEC-ADPMEM-001 "Memory adapter: peek and settle"
context Toolchain
aggregate Adapters
type infrastructure
status agreed

construct:
  handler at adapters/memory/src/index.ts
  touches adapters/memory/**
  needs SPEC-RT-002
  Add `observes = { diff: "native", state: true }` to the adapter: stopCapture and peekCapture
  report what was published in the window, read() reports the whole log.
  peekCapture(): while a window is open return the records stopCapture would return right now,
  in the same order and shape, without moving the window or consuming anything; with no window
  open return []. Delivered stimuli and seeded records are never in it (the stopCapture rule).
  settle(): resolve false when no window is open; otherwise yield the event loop once
  (setImmediate) and resolve true. It never writes to the log (the memory adapter needs no
  sentinel: its log is its own).
  reset() closes the window, so a peek after reset is [].

enforce:
  peekCapture returns the in-window records without consuming them
  peekCapture returns [] when no window is open
  settle resolves true only with a window open, after yielding the event loop
  settle resolves false when no window is open

contract:
  input ObserveInput
  response ObserveResult

scenario "a peek reports the window's effects and consumes nothing":
  when: ObserveMemory { script: "start deliver:Ping peek peek stop" }
  predict success:
    response OK ObserveResult { trace: "start deliver:Ping peek=1 peek=1 stop=1", lastTypes: "Pong", peekEqualsStop: true }
    filesystem has []

scenario "a peek before any effect is empty":
  when: ObserveMemory { script: "start peek stop" }
  predict success:
    response OK ObserveResult { trace: "start peek=0 stop=0" }
    filesystem has []

scenario "the delivered stimulus is not in a peek, only what the consumer published":
  when: ObserveMemory { script: "start deliver:Ping peek" }
  predict success:
    response OK ObserveResult { trace: "start deliver:Ping peek=1", lastTypes: "Pong" }
    filesystem has []

scenario "seeded records are not in a peek":
  when: ObserveMemory { script: "seed start peek stop" }
  predict success:
    response OK ObserveResult { trace: "seed start peek=0 stop=0" }
    filesystem has []

scenario "a peek after stop finds the window closed":
  when: ObserveMemory { script: "start deliver:Ping stop peek" }
  predict success:
    response OK ObserveResult { trace: "start deliver:Ping stop=1 peek=0" }
    filesystem has []

scenario "reset closes the window":
  when: ObserveMemory { script: "start deliver:Ping reset peek" }
  predict success:
    response OK ObserveResult { trace: "start deliver:Ping reset peek=0" }
    filesystem has []

scenario "settle vouches once the consumer's publishes are in the log":
  when: ObserveMemory { script: "start deliver:Ping settle peek stop" }
  predict success:
    response OK ObserveResult { trace: "start deliver:Ping settle=true peek=1 stop=1" }
    filesystem has []

scenario "settle declines when no window is open":
  when: ObserveMemory { script: "settle" }
  predict success:
    response OK ObserveResult { trace: "settle=false" }
    filesystem has []

scenario "settle vouches on an empty window, which is how an absence is proven":
  when: ObserveMemory { script: "start settle stop" }
  predict success:
    response OK ObserveResult { trace: "start settle=true stop=0" }
    filesystem has []
